,title,link,text,language,family
0,Guiyang Miao language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guiyang_Miao_language,"Guiyang Miao, also known as Guiyang Hmong, is a Miao language of China. It is named after Guiyang, Guizhou, though not all varieties are spoken there. The endonym is Hmong, a name it shares with the Hmong language.","Miao, Southwestern Guiyang",Hmong-Mien
1,Hmong-Mien languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hmong–Mien_languages,"The Hmong-Mien languages (also known as Miao-Yao and rarely as Yangtzean) [1] are a highly tonal language family of southern China and northern Southeast Asia. They are spoken in mountainous areas of southern China, including Guizhou, Hunan, Yunnan, Sichuan, Guangxi, Guangdong and Hubei provinces. The speakers of these languages are predominantly ""hill people"", in contrast to the ...","Miao, Southwestern Guiyang",Hmong-Mien
2,"Miao People's Ancient Ethnic Song ""Maple Song"" | Chinese Ethnic Music",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=b83_E2mrPCw,"Miao is a Chinese term, while the component groups of people have their own autonyms, such as (with some variant spellings) Hmong, Hmu, Xong (Qo-Xiong), and A-Hmao.","Miao, Southwestern Guiyang",Hmong-Mien
3,Huaxi Flower Hmong (Hmou) Music | Flower Hmong Tribe in Guiyang | XY,https://xy3mas93.bandcamp.com/album/huaxi-flower-hmong-hmou-music,"Huaxi Flower Hmong is one of these dialects, with approximately 4,000 speakers. Guiyang Hmong is also called Hmou, as a distinct Miao or Hmong tribe with their unique language and costume. They use several traditional instruments, including the Mimi (also known as Zimeixiao 姊妹箫 in Chinese), the Khen, and the Xiaotong (a type of flute).","Miao, Southwestern Guiyang",Hmong-Mien
4,Guiyang Miao language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/guiyang_miao_language,"Guiyang Miao, also known as Guiyang Hmong, refers to a branch of the Hmongic languages within the Hmong-Mien (Miao-Yao) language family, spoken primarily by members of the Miao ethnic group in Guizhou Province, southwestern China. [1] This branch encompasses several closely related but distinct varieties, including Hmong Njua, Horned Miao, Sinicized Miao, Gha-mu, Diandongbei-Large Flowery Miao ...","Miao, Southwestern Guiyang",Hmong-Mien
5,Ancient folk songs of the Miao ethnic group in Xifeng - China Daily,https://www.chinadaily.com.cn/m/guizhou/guiyang/2021-03/31/content_37543772.htm,"Miao people living in the Xiwang Mountain area in Xifeng county of Guiyang, the capital city of Guizhou province, are divided into three branches - the Xiaohua Miao, Qing Miao and Chuan Miao.","Miao, Southwestern Guiyang",Hmong-Mien
6,"Full article: We know who they are, because of what they sing: Miao ...",https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/17411912.2024.2391125,"Introduction From 2010 to 2016, I, Mofang Yuan, taught Chinese folk song singing at a music school in Changsha, Hunan province, China. Some of my students belonged to the Miao ethnic group. Through conversations with them, I gained insights into Miao culture and their songs, sparking my interest in delving deeper into the music of this minority group. Equipped with a basic knowledge of Miao ...","Miao, Southwestern Guiyang",Hmong-Mien
7,Lanmo - Ethnic Minority Music in Guizhou I,https://xy3mas93.bandcamp.com/album/lanmo-ethnic-minority-music-in-guizhou-i,"Lanmo - Ethnic Minority Music in Guizhou I by Guizhou Ethnic Minority Artists, released 21 January 2026 1. Hmu Morning at Miao Mountains 2. Kaili Hmu Love Song 3. Kaili Hmu Khen Cloud Tune 4. Hmu Flying Song 5. Zhenning Black Hmu Season Song 6. Zhenning Black Hmu Visiting Song 7. Haipa Hmu Khen 8. Green Hmu Ancient Song 9. Hmu Drum & Khen Ceremony 10. Western Bouyei Lanmo Song 11. Western ...","Miao, Southwestern Guiyang",Hmong-Mien
8,"Miao, Southwestern Guiyang Language (HMG) - Ethnologue",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/hmg/,"Southwestern Guiyang Miao is a stable indigenous language of China. It belongs to the Hmong-Mien language family and is part of the Hmong macrolanguage. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools.","Miao, Southwestern Guiyang",Hmong-Mien
9,Hmong/Miao songs - YouTube Music,https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLp5I0Och-TvhYQy8CNIVO_GDQh9UC8Ggh,"All songs were found on Youtube, all credit goes to their rightful owners and song makers. I do not take any credit.","Miao, Southwestern Guiyang",Hmong-Mien
